        "original_id": "ca95ec8a-acc3-5cb1-8e1a-f8109f0e8fe4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charlie Kendall, Donald Sterling, Bobby Samini, Danilo Gallinari\n- Organizations: Los Angeles Clippers, National Basketball Association, TMZ\n- Roles: businessman, owner, lead counsel, basketball player\n- Events: proposed team purchase, litigation\n\nFacts:\n- Donald Sterling, born Donald Tokowitz on April 26, 1934, is a Jewish-American businessman.\n- In 1982, Charlie Kendall was reportedly interested in purchasing the Los Angeles Clippers from owner Donald Sterling, but Donald Sterling did not sell the team.\n- Bobby Samini served as lead counsel to former Los Angeles Clippers owner Donald Sterling in highly publicized litigation involving the National Basketball Association, TMZ, and V. Stiviano.\n- Danilo Gallinari, born on August 8, 1988, is an Italian professional basketball player for the Los Angeles Clippers of the National Basketball Association.",
